sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/darwin1859-ch04-06> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch04-06--grok> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch04-06--grok> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 on darwin1859-ch04-06: partially-resolvable, resolvability 0.56" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.1.0> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.1.0" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.561"^^xsd:double ;
    delphi:hasVerdict "partially-resolvable" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.64"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "Mating system and weapon presence are standard comparative variables with an obvious phylogenetic contrast, and the trees needed to run it are public. The trait columns themselves still have to be compiled, especially for combat frequency, so the work is months of harmonization rather than a download. Within mammals the test would be informative, with the usual confound that horns and large males are not used only for fighting." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: Code mating system, male-combat frequency, and presence of weapons, then fit a phylogenetic regression. The claim would be confirmed if polygynous lineages have higher combat rates and weapon frequencies than monogamous relatives after body size and habitat are controlled; it would be refuted if weapon evolution is independent of mating system. Combat itself is usually proxied by weaponry and sexual size dimorphism." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "Mating system and weapon inventories are spread through handbooks and supplements rather than one global table.", "Weapons proxy fighting and can also function in display or predator defence.", "Birds are less consistently coded than large mammals." ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/darwin1859-ch04-06--grok--dataset-1>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/darwin1859-ch04-06--grok--dataset-2>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/darwin1859-ch04-06--grok--dataset-3> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch04-06--grok--operationalizability> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Operationalizability of darwin1859-ch04-06 by Grok 4.7: 0.76" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.1.0-operationalizability> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.1.0/operationalizability" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.76"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:isPartOf <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch04-06--grok> ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> .
